<div class="side-by-side">
  <h2>The Challenge</h2>

  <p>
    Honkai: Star Rail was launching a collaboration with Fortnite, and the
    launch window was short. The goal was to build awareness for the collab,
    drive players to buy and use the new Honkai: Star Rail skins in Fortnite,
    and bridge two fanbases that had little overlap, all in a single moment.
  </p>
</div>

<h2>The Solution</h2>

<div class="side-by-side">
  <figure>
    <img
      src="/assets/img/projects/astral-rift-rumble/format.webp"
      alt="Format graphic for Astral Rift Rumble: two teams of seven players, four 20-minute rounds, and the team with the most round wins takes the title"
      width="768"
      height="432"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </figure>
  <div>
    <p class="big">A friendly showdown built for two audiences</p>
    <p>
      We paired Fortnite icons Ninja and Clix with beloved Honkai: Star Rail
      creators and split them into Team Kafka and Team Blade for a 7v7 zone
      control match. The format stayed easy for casual viewers to follow while
      keeping enough competitive structure to hold energy through a two-hour
      broadcast.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="side-by-side">
  <div>
    <p class="big">14 creators, one unified moment</p>
    <p>
      We targeted 14 creators across both communities and streamed them
      simultaneously, multi-streaming to vertical platforms where possible and
      categorizing every stream under Fortnite so the collab reached the game’s
      existing audience. Creator-facing guides for stream setup and overlays,
      plus tech checks ahead of show day, kept every channel consistent and
      on-brand.
    </p>
  </div>
  <figure>
    <img
      src="/assets/img/projects/astral-rift-rumble/hosts.webp"
